# Small things in October

A fictional month, October 1–31, 2026. These are sample entries, not anyone's private writing. The scenes keep sentences from the entries; the pictures, recordings and objects are demonstration assets. Media references name real works, but no account activity or live service lookup is claimed.

The main demo is public and unencrypted; the mixed demo also contains protected entries and attachments. A scratchpad or a hidden comment is still in the file. See the separate demo guide for saving, protection, offline reading and tools that need your own action.

The file on this page is **{{document.filename}}**. Begin with [the first morning](#2026-10-01), visit [the garden model](#garden-model), or come back to [the month in numbers](#october-walks).

:::record scale #attention-scale
name: attention-to-small-things
kind: ordinal
minimum: 1
maximum: 5
anchor-low: noticed almost nothing
anchor-high: noticed many small details
:::

### 2026-10-01 | A window to begin with

.0830 - KITCHEN

Rain traced crooked lines down the kitchen window while my mug of tea cooled on the wooden table. The lamp was still on, a small yellow circle beside the blue notebook. I cut the last slice of bread and watched the garden tree let go of one leaf at a time.

I wanted a record of the ordinary bits: **warm bread**, *wet leaves*, and ==a whole quiet minute== before the kettle clicked. Nothing dramatic happened. That felt like enough to write down. #home @kitchen

[x] Put a fresh notebook on the table #home
[ ] Mend the loose button on my coat #mending
[!] Return the borrowed garden key #garden
[>] Move the shelf sketch to [Saturday](#2026-10-03) #making
[<] Pick up the library reservation on October 4 #reading
[-] Buy a second kettle #home
o 18:30 Soup with Robin
? Would a shelf beside the window make room for the notebook
! Keep a pencil in the kitchen drawer
= Tea, rain and a page to begin with.

[[ The first line was written while the toast was still warm. ]]

