### 2026-10-03 | The corner café
@setting: media/scene-2026-10-03.json

The café window had steamed over, except for a clear patch just above our table. Robin drew a wobbly shelf on a paper napkin while I held a mug of tea between my hands. A small vase of flowers leaned toward the lamp behind the counter.

We decided the shelf could wait until we found wood we liked. I took the napkin home inside my notebook, next to [the question from Thursday](#2026-10-01). The useful part of the morning was having time to sit there. #making #friends @cafe

| Shelf idea | What I liked | What can wait |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Narrow, by the window | Room for one notebook | Choosing the wood |
| Hooks underneath | A place for the garden key | Measuring the wall |

[ ] Measure the kitchen wall #making
  Start with the space beside the window, then check where the lamp plugs in.

