### 2026-10-04 | A book by the window
@setting: media/scene-2026-10-04.json

The library had a green chair between a tall bookshelf and the window. I sat there with a book open on my knees while the rain tapped the glass. Someone had left a tiny paper boat on the low table, so I turned it carefully and put it back where it was.

Reading [Pride and Prejudice](https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66554W) again, slowly. I had forgotten how much of it happens in conversations that seem to be about something else. I wrote ++read the awkward pauses too++ in the notebook.[^library-chair] #reading @library

[^library-chair]: The chair, library and visit are fictional. The linked book is Jane Austen's real novel; the link is a reference, not an attached copy.

[x] Pick up the reserved book #reading

