### 2026-10-07 | What a leaf remembers
@setting: media/scene-2026-10-07.json
@hand: default
@ink: default

The park bench was dry enough for a book and a notebook this afternoon. I picked up a yellow leaf under the tree and held it against the sky until I could see its little branches of veins. The river beyond the flowers was moving faster than it looked from the bridge.

At home I left the leaf beside the desk lamp and made a question card from something I had been reading. Turning it over is more fun than immediately looking up the answer. #learning #walks @park

:::record card #leaf-card
label: One question from the park
front: What does a leaf make from light, water and air?
back: |
  Sugars, with oxygen released along the way.
  The yellow leaf on the desk made me think about the green ones still outside.
:::

