### 2026-10-09 | Away for the afternoon
@timezone: Europe/Paris

The train slid into the station under a bright glass roof. I found a seat by the window with my notebook on the little table and a mug of tea warming my hands. Trees, gardens and a red bicycle on a platform passed by in short, disconnected pictures.

At the other end Robin met me beside a market stall piled with apples. We carried bread to a café and watched a little boat move along the river. This fictional day uses an explicit entry timezone; the earlier days keep the document's London timezone. #travel #friends @station

