### 2026-10-16 | The gallery room

The gallery had one wooden bench in front of an easel holding an unfinished painting. A lamp lit the corner of the canvas, and the room's big window framed the top of a tree. I left my notebook closed for a while and looked at the same blue shape until it seemed less like a shape and more like water.

Afterward Robin and I sat at a café table with two mugs of tea. We disagreed about which picture we liked, which gave us something better to talk about than whether the visit had been worth it. #drawing #friends @gallery

::voice ROWAN

(remembering the quiet room)

I liked the space around the painting as much as the painting itself.

