### 2026-10-17 | Apples at the market

The market stall had apples stacked in shallow wooden boxes and flowers tied in paper. I balanced a loaf of bread against my notebook while Robin found the smallest bag of pears. Behind the stall, a bicycle leaned against a tree with a basket full of folded cloth.

At home I put the fruit on the kitchen table and made tea. The red apples looked especially bright beside the blue mug. I saved a few ordinary details in a list instead of trying to turn the morning into a story. #food #friends @market

- the stripe on the paper flower wrapper
- a bicycle bell from the next stall
- bread still warm through the bag
  - the corner Robin tore off on the walk home

1. Put the pears in the bowl.
2. Keep two apples for tomorrow.
3. Leave the notebook on the table.

