### 2026-10-20 | Clay on the table

At the workshop table I rolled a little clay bowl with a rim as uneven as the river bank. Robin set a mug of tea beside the lamp, safely away from the tools. Through the window I could see the garden flowers nodding while the potter opened the back door.

I drew the bowl in my notebook before leaving it to dry. What I thought would be a five-minute job turned into a whole afternoon of making the same curve over and over. The unfinished shape was the part I wanted to keep. #making #drawing @workshop

:::record reflection #clay-note
