### 2026-10-24 | The bench was empty

Fog softened the far side of the river this morning. I sat on the park bench with my notebook and tea mug, looking at the tree above the boat landing. A bicycle went past so quietly that I noticed its light before I heard its wheels.

I forgot to note the length of the walk, so the distance stays empty. There were no new flowers in the little patch by the bench, and I wrote zero for that count because zero is what I meant. An empty space and a zero tell different stories. #walks @park

