### 2026-10-29 | After dark

The river was almost black tonight, except where the park lamp made a long yellow stripe. Robin and I sat on the bench under the tree with tea mugs from the café. A boat knocked once against the landing and then went quiet; the moon made the bicycle's metal bell look white.

I opened the notebook but could not see the lines, so I closed it again. This is the part I remembered when I got home: the small sound of the boat, the warm mug, and Robin pointing at a star I had not noticed. #outside #friends @river

:::record measurement #walk-29
