### 2026-10-31 | A month on the table

In the morning I spread the notebook, the library book and the folded café napkin across the kitchen table. The lamp was on, the tea mug was warm, and sunlight came through the window onto the clay bowl. The bare tree outside made a much simpler drawing than the one I had begun with.

There is a month here now: rain and bread, a little travel, a bowl, some unfinished things. I can follow a tag or a link instead of reading straight through. I still like [the first morning](#2026-10-01) best, because it did not know what would come next. #home #writing @kitchen

